# Desktop launcher bats (Mike workflow)

Global copy: `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\plugins\local\n78-global-rules\rules\desktop-launcher-bats.mdc` — edit the repo file, then `run-updocs.ps1 -SyncMirrors` (or install-n78-cursor-standards.ps1).

Canonical spine: `reference/NIVO78_DESKTOP_LAUNCH.txt` and `N78-Ops/tools/lib/N78DesktopLaunch.ps1`.

## Fixed build / install / shortcut — mandatory for all desktop apps

Every Nivo78 **Windows desktop** app MUST use **the same three fixed layers** every release. Paths MUST NOT move when TFM, RID, Gradle folders, or CI output layout changes.

**Operator Desktop `.lnk`** = `%ProgramFiles%\{InstallFolderName}\{ExeFileName}` only (stamped `ShortcutUseInstallExe = $true`). **Never** point the operator `.lnk` at the repo clone, `:desktop:run` output, or `bin\Release\net*-windows\…`.

**Engineering only:** `ensure-{product}-launch.ps1`, `tools\launchers\{Prefix}.bat`, `Desktop\Apps\…` twins, and optional `br` / `:desktop:run` — they MUST still write to the **profile-defined fixed repo distributable folder**, then **sync** to Program Files before the shortcut is “latest.”

| Layer | Rule |
| ----- | ---- |
| **Repo build** | .NET: fixed `OutputPath` (e.g. `bin\run\`), `AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath=false`, `AppendRuntimeIdentifierToOutputPath=false`. Profile `DotNetOutputRelative` must match. KMP: fixed Gradle distributable folder in `N78DesktopLaunchProfile.ps1` (`GradlePackageFolder`). |
| **Install** | `%ProgramFiles%\{InstallFolderName}\{ExeFileName}` via `sync-{product}-install.ps1` only. |
| **Desktop .lnk** | `{ProgramFiles}\{InstallFolderName}\{ExeFileName}` when `ShortcutUseInstallExe` (N78-Ops family default). Launch `.bat` twins are for repo/Apps — not the operator Desktop `.lnk` target. |
| **Repo / Apps twins** | `tools\launchers\{Prefix}.bat` and `Desktop\Apps\…` call `ensure-*-launch.ps1` — never hard-code a moving build path. |

When adding or changing a desktop product, verify `create-desktop-shortcuts.ps1` was run after profile changes so the desktop icon matches the table above.

## Two launch paths for new runnables

When you add a **new runnable** artifact the user will use more than once — desktop app entry, dev utility, maintain script with a launcher, test helper, etc. — **always** ship **two** launch paths in the **same turn**:

1. **Canonical launcher** in the repo (e.g. `tools/launchers/{Name}.bat` or `code/tools/launchers/…`) — relative paths, portable within the clone.
2. **Apps twin** at `%USERPROFILE%\Desktop\Apps\{same path as under Desktop\Nivo78}\{Name}.bat` — store apps at `Desktop\Apps\N78-APA\`, business apps at `Desktop\Apps\Business\N78-Foo\`. Create the folder if it is missing.

Skip the Apps twin only when the user explicitly says no desktop shortcut, or the tool is clearly one-off / internal with no user-facing run intent.

Do **not** drop twins on the Desktop root or into `Desktop\Bats`.

## Desktop bat template (N78-APA on this PC)

```bat
@echo off
rem Desktop Apps launcher — {one-line purpose}
setlocal
set "REPO=C:\Users\Mike\Desktop\Nivo78\N78-APA"
set "LAUNCHER=%REPO%\tools\launchers\{CanonicalName}.bat"
if not exist "%LAUNCHER%" (
 echo Could not find %LAUNCHER%
 echo Update REPO in this bat file if your N78-APA folder moved.
 pause
 exit /b 1
)
call "%LAUNCHER%" %*
set "ERR=%ERRORLEVEL%"
if %ERR% NEQ 0 pause
endlocal & exit /b %ERR%
```

For PowerShell-only tools, call the `.ps1` under `tools/maintain/` instead of a repo `.bat`, same `REPO` block and error `pause`.

## Naming

- **User-facing / solo-operator tools:** plain names inside `Desktop\Apps\N78-{Product}\` (e.g. `APA-View-Backup.bat`) — no extra `N78-` on the bat unless the product name includes it.
- **Repo maintainers / release:** keep existing `N78-APA-*` names under `tools/launchers/` when that matches repo convention.

## Checklist when closing

- [ ] Fixed repo output path documented in profile / project file (no TFM/RID suffix in shortcut targets)
- [ ] Desktop `.lnk` uses fixed Program Files `{ExeFileName}` (or documented override)
- [ ] Canonical launcher exists and was tested once from repo path
- [ ] Apps twin `.bat` created or updated under `Desktop\Apps\{N78-Product}\` with correct `REPO` and target
- [ ] Closing summary mentions both paths
